RECORDED – 8.1.17 download of a queue file INUBIT does not have, in an existing workflow
(exit 0, neutralized). INUBIT answers both parts with the exception chain
java.lang.RuntimeException>com.inubit.ibis.utils.InubitException and a two-line message
"Exception from service object: @Start@Unable to download@@@Unable to download@End@<path>",
the path naming owner, workflow, state and file (.wfsp for the variables). Expected: the
marker "@Start@Unable to download" classifies both parts NotFound.

Frames use the fixed nonce 0123456789abcdef0123456789abcdef; a replay replaces it with the
nonce of its request. The recording has no vendor noise lines.
Used by QueueEntryHelperClassifierTest and CliQueueEntryAdapterTest (tasks.md T019, T035,
research D-5, D-21).
